{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788306621,"nonce":"mCso3EOtp7lNcuVHjIFHFeLYDqk=","message":"REWRITTEN CONTRACT — supersedes the Acceptance in #0 and the criteria amended in #5, #6 and #7. Planner session for this issue, 2026-09-01, against main `3158c5a` (280fb78 merged). Evan's direction, verbatim: \"run m1 with the intention to thrive not just survive\"; \"raise to 20 days, a real food cycle and test to see if they can set themselves up for success\"; \"we want a nice base, farm, and militia\"; \"no prison is fine\". Reasoning for every decision below is in DESIGN's decisions log (2026-09-01, M1 re-plan).\n\n## Goal\n\nTwenty in-game days (1,200,000 ticks) under agent control on a fresh crash-landing: nobody is lost, and the colony ends with a farm that feeds it, a workshop, a rec room, a barracks it built itself, and an armed militia that has met a raid. \"See what you can come up with\" is the instruction to the agent; the two tables below are what gets graded.\n\n## Dependencies\n\n- `main` at or after `3158c5a` with its `Build:` commit, and `accept/280fb78-wake-halts.py` green on a bench. Every other gate item is merged and bench-proven: `61794cd`, `40ed42f`, `722c951`, `b1b3060`, `7382bdd`, `1113019`, `2d9a1da`, `261f2e9`, and `1adc737`'s `build` / `place-layout`.\n- Not dependencies, filed for the proofs they sharpen: `ae78ecc` (the records read) and `47547ca` (the armour read). Each row below names its fallback read.\n\n## Fixture and staging\n\n- `_RimWorld-Agent --quicktest`: Crashlanded, Cassandra, Rough, 250x250, random tile. Reroll until `digest.site.biome` is `TemperateForest` and `digest.posture` shows at least two violence-capable colonists. Record the reroll count.\n- Staging, every step a `dev` row: the base room — one enclosed room, three beds, a heat source — placed with `buildable:true` and clean under `site-audit`; `dev:starter-kit {preset:\"shelter\"}` away from